=== Governors ===
The elections for governors took place in ten provinces in September, which were won in six provinces by Kirchner's [[Front for Victory]]. [[Hermes Binner]] was elected [[governor of Santa Fe]], defeating Peronist [[Rafael Bielsa]], the former [[Foreign relations of Argentina|Minister of Foreign Affairs]] for Pres. Néstor Kirchner. Binner thus became the first [[Socialist Party (Argentina)|Socialist]] governor in Argentina's history and the first non-[[Justicialism|Justicialist]] elected governor of that province. Center-left [[Fabiana Ríos]] ([[Support for an Egalitarian Republic|ARI]]) became the first woman elected governor in Argentina, winning an upset in [[Tierra del Fuego Province (Argentina)|Tierra del Fuego Province]], while the moderately conservative [[Mauricio Macri]] was elected [[List of Mayors and Chiefs of Government of Buenos Aires|Mayor of Buenos Aires]] (an office similar to governor) in June 2007.<ref name=Mde>[https://www.lemonde.fr/ameriques/article/2007/09/04/pour-la-premiere-fois-un-socialiste-est-elu-gouverneur-d-une-province-argentine_951026_3222.html Pour la première fois, un socialiste est élu gouverneur d'une province argentine], ''[[Le Monde]]'', September 4, 2007 {{in lang|fr}}</ref>

[[Corrientes Province]] and [[Santiago del Estero Province]] did not have elections for governors in 2007, as they had already taken place in 2005.

